WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.483
[MUSIC]

00:00:04.483 --> 00:00:10.063
[APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; China's one

00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:15.940
child policy is regarded as the biggest
social experiment in the human history.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.475
I'm honored to be a subject
in this experiment.

00:00:18.475 --> 00:00:22.570
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I am one of the 150 million,

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:23.969
only children in my generation.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.570
In 2015,
when I first came to United States for

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:33.560
business school, China dropped
the one child policy after 35 years.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:38.233
Many GSB classmates showed great
empathy to me, saying, Yourng, I'm so

00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:42.179
happy for you that China eventually
dropped this evil policy.

00:00:42.179 --> 00:00:45.690
How could the Chinese government
deny human rights like that?

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.110
It must have been really hard for
you growing up without siblings, I cannot

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:55.280
imagine that people could not make their
own choices about how many kids to have.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:01.420
I really appreciated their compassion,
but deep inside I feel conflicted.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.197
There's some other classmates for

00:01:03.197 --> 00:01:06.440
they asked,
how do you view the one child policy?

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.832
Was it good or bad?

00:01:08.832 --> 00:01:09.723
My response.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:12.375
I don't know.

00:01:12.375 --> 00:01:14.342
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Since then,

00:01:14.342 --> 00:01:18.930
I have tried to learn more in hopes
of arriving at a better answer.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.100
Today, let me start with my
own story as the only child.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.160
Try to imagine,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.620
that you are a five year old only child,
living in China, like I was.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:35.120
I have to tell you, that you have to spend
some time alone, talking to yourself,

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.020
playing by yourself,
sometimes even hugging yourself.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:42.785
Because, you have to play two roles in
the same time, princess, and the prince.

00:01:42.785 --> 00:01:46.990
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But trust me, life was not that bad.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:48.060
I had a great time,

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:54.110
I had great companionship with my
cousins and neighborhood kids.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:00.200
And I probably have to admit that I cannot
understand the whole concept of siblings,

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.940
because all of my peers
are only children as well.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.219
So the idea of having a sibling
never crossed my mind.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:13.630
At school we were taught that the one
child policy was fundamentally important

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:20.140
to China, to keep the population a great
size and to ensure the quality of life.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.580
At home my mom,

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:26.920
who has three other siblings,
tell me a story about back in the 1960s.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:30.160
Four of them had to split
one loaf of bread for

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:35.020
a meal, all her clothes are pass
downs from her two elder sisters.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.246
I also heard stories from
people of my own age.

00:02:40.246 --> 00:02:44.992
The euro part of China, where the
one-child policy had not been enforced,

00:02:44.992 --> 00:02:49.530
girls had to give away opportunities for
education for the boys at home.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.160
So with all these stories in mind,

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:57.640
I truly believe that the one child
policy was the right way to go.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:03.180
For me, for my family,
as well as for my family,

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.690
until one day in 2013, I was still
working in China as a sales manager.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:11.040
Riding a bullet train from
Beijing from Shanghai,

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.770
I got a long message from my
mom which was very unusual.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:18.910
She wrote that, she had been diagnosed
with a heart disease called HDD,

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:22.530
and she needed open chest
surgery as soon as possible.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:28.856
She had hesitated to tell me because
my work schedule is full, but she

00:03:28.856 --> 00:03:34.942
eventually decided to let me know, because
the risk of the surgery is super high.

00:03:36.956 --> 00:03:43.799
So at that moment actually I was on
the business trip with several colleagues,

00:03:43.799 --> 00:03:48.980
and also my clients sitting
right in front of me.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:54.514
But I burst into tears, I was terrified by
the thought what could happen to my mom.

00:03:54.514 --> 00:04:01.430
I also felt troubled how could my mom
hesitate to tell me I was her only child.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:05.899
I should be the person to keep
company with her, care of here, and

00:04:05.899 --> 00:04:08.846
sign under the conscious for the surgery.

00:04:08.846 --> 00:04:14.233
But at that moment, she was still
thinking about disturbing my work,

00:04:14.233 --> 00:04:15.915
this is ridiculous.

00:04:15.915 --> 00:04:22.100
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; So I look outside of this plain window,

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:26.860
feel terrified, hopeless and
as well as obligated.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:31.040
And for the very first time I
wished I could have a sibling

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.490
to share this fear and
overcome the hardship together.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:39.980
So a few months later,
I get back to my hometown,

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:45.120
I was very happy to spend more time
with my mom and family members.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:45.990
But in the meantime,

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:51.060
I was also struggled with handling
with both of her and my work.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:58.800
So I'm very lucky because the surgery was
very successful and my mom recovered.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:03.740
However, I kept to thinking about
this idea of having a sibling,

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:07.080
how could my life be different
if I was not the only child?

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:12.224
Recently, I send this question to
over 100 only child friends in China,

00:05:12.224 --> 00:05:15.960
here are some responses are really
interesting, I will share with you.

00:05:18.769 --> 00:05:22.142
If I were not the only child,
I wouldn't be forced to go on so

00:05:22.142 --> 00:05:24.335
many blind dates set up by my parents.

00:05:24.335 --> 00:05:26.644
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; However,

00:05:26.644 --> 00:05:30.894
my parents wouldn't be able to pay for
the down payments for

00:05:30.894 --> 00:05:36.252
a new apartment for me, which is regarded
as a must to get married in China.

00:05:36.252 --> 00:05:39.948
Here is one struck me most I
might not be as successful

00:05:39.948 --> 00:05:44.148
as I am because I couldn't
monopolize all the attention and

00:05:44.148 --> 00:05:47.390
resources from my parents.,
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:50.520
&gt;&gt; But I would be more free living abroad,

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.620
marrying to my same sex partner,

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.280
instead of living the life to
meet my parents expectations.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:02.130
My friends are as conflicted as I am,
the good is inseparable from the bad.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.530
Scholars have examined the one child
policy from many different perspectives.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:13.457
Criticizing the policy for violating
human rights or creating big social

00:06:13.457 --> 00:06:18.199
issues such as, Little Emperor Syndrome
aka China's spoiled brats.

00:06:18.199 --> 00:06:20.808
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; As a little emperor myself,

00:06:20.808 --> 00:06:25.550
I'm very grateful for all the privileges
I've received as an only child.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:31.210
Especially for the improved opportunities
for women, however, I have to admit that

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:35.760
the excessive love and
attention also creates larger pressure.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:41.580
After the termination of the one child
policy I had a conversation with my mom.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.390
How many kids do you think I should have,
I asked?

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:50.940
She urge me to have at least the two
in light of all the downside of being

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.440
an only child.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:56.900
But I'm not sure, since that I can
imagine that my future husband and

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:59.990
I have to support four elderly parents.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:02.999
I think two or more kids, that's crazy.

00:07:02.999 --> 00:07:07.703
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And especially given the social

00:07:07.703 --> 00:07:13.666
expectation for taking care of a parent
is way much higher in China's culture.

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:17.967
And what [INAUDIBLE] me more is the
thought that if something bad falls on me,

00:07:17.967 --> 00:07:20.550
what could happen to my mom.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:24.279
I cannot imagine what my mom would go
through if she lost her only child.

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:29.610
My stepfather is a sociologist
specializing in the study of families

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.620
who lost their only child.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:36.250
He told me that now there are more than
one million such families in China.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:40.840
These parents generally are too old
to give another birth to the baby so

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.896
they lost their only hope.

00:07:42.896 --> 00:07:49.420
Many of suffer from tremendous
emotional trauma and

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:53.690
irrecoverable hardships in
terms of finance and also life.

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:59.270
So I think this helps me to
explain part of my survey.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:03.640
Why my generation carries
a heavier emotional burden, and

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:05.320
he is less willing to take risks?

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:08.840
Was the one child policy good or bad?

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.960
To be honest I still don't
have the answer, but

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.960
here is the lesson I
want to share with you.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:21.360
When you're from the outside it seems
easy to evaluate a government policy or

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.470
a business decision that
had impact on other people.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:30.190
Once you move to the inside it's
not just like snap your finger and

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.380
get to the answer to that question.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.860
So I would urge you and myself,
think about the big choices and

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:40.660
decisions on the individual level.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.660
Consider life stories.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.270
And when you have the power
to make decisions for

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:50.100
large groups of people, no matter you
are a political leader or business leader.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.740
Try to take on the view from the inside,

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:56.580
do not let the view from
the outside dominate your choice.

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:00.216
And this is my lesson from
the one child policy, thank you.

00:09:00.216 --> 00:09:01.852
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:09:01.852 --> 00:09:06.399
[MUSIC]

